From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burntcarrot <aadhav.n1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Mar 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] runsc: fix seccomp filters, scheduler idle advance, add dst/BUILD

Three runtime fixes discovered during gVisor backend testing:

1. Sentry seccomp filter: add SYS_ACCEPT4 (MatchAll) and SYS_GETSOCKNAME
   (MatchAll) to the base allowedSyscalls. Go 1.22+ uses accept4 instead
   of accept in the net package. Previously accept4 was only allowed via
   controlServerFilters(fd) with a specific fd. getsockname is needed by
   the urpc/control server path after accepting connections.

2. Gofer seccomp filter: add SYS_ACCEPT4 (MatchAll) to the base
   allowedSyscalls. Previously accept4 was only in udsCreateSyscalls
   which requires UDSCreateEnabled=true (not the default).

3. DST scheduler idle advance: when all goroutines are sleeping (waiting
   on timers), the idle loop previously blocked on <-ds.wakeup indefinitely.
   The virtual clock never advanced, timers never fired, and the system
   deadlocked. Fix: add time.After(10ms) branch that calls AdvanceQuantum()
   to advance the virtual clock and wake sleeping goroutines.

Also includes nil-guard fixes in taskYielded() and dstYield() for tasks
that are not registered with the DST scheduler, plus minor code cleanup
and import fixes (syscall instead of linuxerr, local clock constants).
